{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XvqfK5X6MD14iL9pT4QrPj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://opengitops.dev/\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T22:30:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"OpenGitOps (CNCF sandbox project)\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: [\"D3 Application Delivery\"]\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"gitops\", \"declarative\", \"versioned-immutable\", \"pulled-automatically\", \"continuously-reconciled\"]\n7\t---\n8\t# OpenGitOps Principles v1.0.0 (opengitops.dev)\n9\t\n10\tOpenGitOps is a set of open-source standards, best practices, and community-focused education to help organizations adopt a structured, standardized approach to implementing GitOps.\n11\t\n12\tGitOps is a set of principles for operating and managing software systems. The desired state of a GitOps managed system must be:\n13\t\n14\t1. **Declarative** — A system managed by GitOps must have its desired state expressed declaratively.\n15\t2. **Versioned and Immutable** — Desired state is stored in a way that enforces immutability, versioning and retains a complete version history.\n16\t3. **Pulled Automatically** — Software agents automatically pull the desired state declarations from the source.\n17\t4. **Continuously Reconciled** — Software agents continuously observe actual system state and attempt to apply the desired state.\n18\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b4f5a06-4bc3-4221-b900-b8461cc3e79d","uuid":"56843130-f12e-4d59-b154-c78dec0350c6","timestamp":"2026-08-31T10:04:19.952Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\opengitops-principles-2026-08-23.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://opengitops.dev/\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T22:30:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"OpenGitOps (CNCF sandbox project)\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"D3 Application Delivery\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"gitops\", \"declarative\", \"versioned-immutable\", \"pulled-automatically\", \"continuously-reconciled\"]\n---\n# OpenGitOps Principles v1.0.0 (opengitops.dev)\n\nOpenGitOps is a set of open-source standards, best practices, and community-focused education to help organizations adopt a structured, standardized approach to implementing GitOps.\n\nGitOps is a set of principles for operating and managing software systems. The desired state of a GitOps managed system must be:\n\n1. **Declarative** — A system managed by GitOps must have its desired state expressed declaratively.\n2. **Versioned and Immutable** — Desired state is stored in a way that enforces immutability, versioning and retains a complete version history.\n3. **Pulled Automatically** — Software agents automatically pull the desired state declarations from the source.\n4. **Continuously Reconciled** — Software agents continuously observe actual system state and attempt to apply the desired state.\n","numLines":18,"startLine":1,"totalLines":18}}}
