{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011PBCfAZkDKLZVsxpTPanBA","type":"tool_result","content":"# Automated Sync Policy - Key Excerpts\n\n## Core Functionality\n\"Argo CD has the ability to automatically sync an application when it detects differences between the desired manifests in Git, and the live state in the cluster.\"\n\n## Default Behavior\n\"By default (and as a safety mechanism), automated sync will not delete resources when Argo CD detects the resource is no longer defined in Git.\"\n\n## Configuration Methods\n\nBasic enablement uses:\n```\nspec:\n  syncPolicy:\n    automated: {}\n```\n\nWith explicit control:\n```\nspec:\n  syncPolicy:\n    automated:\n      enabled: true\n```\n\n## Automatic Pruning\nTo enable resource deletion during sync: \"Pruning can also be enabled to happen automatically as part of the automated sync by running: `argocd app set <APPNAME> --auto-prune`\"\n\nOr via manifest:\n```\nspec:\n  syncPolicy:\n    automated:\n      prune: true\n```\n\n## Automatic Self-Healing\n\"By default, changes that are made to the live cluster will not trigger automated sync.\" Enable with: `argocd app set <APPNAME> --self-heal` or:\n```\nspec:\n  syncPolicy:\n    automated:\n      selfHeal: true\n```\n\n## Key Sync Semantics\n- \"An automated sync will only be performed if the application is OutOfSync.\"\n- \"Automatic sync will only attempt one synchronization per unique combination of commit SHA1 and application parameters.\"\n- \"The automatic sync interval...defaults to `120s` with added jitter of `60s` for a maximum period of 3 minutes.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b4f5a06-4bc3-4221-b900-b8461cc3e79d","uuid":"eb2f741b-6373-492f-ae40-39867de7d72a","timestamp":"2026-08-31T10:04:40.729Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":14689,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Automated Sync Policy - Key Excerpts\n\n## Core Functionality\n\"Argo CD has the ability to automatically sync an application when it detects differences between the desired manifests in Git, and the live state in the cluster.\"\n\n## Default Behavior\n\"By default (and as a safety mechanism), automated sync will not delete resources when Argo CD detects the resource is no longer defined in Git.\"\n\n## Configuration Methods\n\nBasic enablement uses:\n```\nspec:\n  syncPolicy:\n    automated: {}\n```\n\nWith explicit control:\n```\nspec:\n  syncPolicy:\n    automated:\n      enabled: true\n```\n\n## Automatic Pruning\nTo enable resource deletion during sync: \"Pruning can also be enabled to happen automatically as part of the automated sync by running: `argocd app set <APPNAME> --auto-prune`\"\n\nOr via manifest:\n```\nspec:\n  syncPolicy:\n    automated:\n      prune: true\n```\n\n## Automatic Self-Healing\n\"By default, changes that are made to the live cluster will not trigger automated sync.\" Enable with: `argocd app set <APPNAME> --self-heal` or:\n```\nspec:\n  syncPolicy:\n    automated:\n      selfHeal: true\n```\n\n## Key Sync Semantics\n- \"An automated sync will only be performed if the application is OutOfSync.\"\n- \"Automatic sync will only attempt one synchronization per unique combination of commit SHA1 and application parameters.\"\n- \"The automatic sync interval...defaults to `120s` with added jitter of `60s` for a maximum period of 3 minutes.\"","durationMs":4803,"url":"https://argo-cd.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user-guide/auto_sync/"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JAFbZsnFSfpg9pxxphsanu","type":"tool_result","content":"# Flux GitOps Toolkit Components\n\n## Source Controllers\n**Description:** \"The GitOps Toolkit Source Controllers documentation.\"\n\n**Custom Resources:**\n- GitRepository CRD\n- OCIRepository CRD\n- HelmRepository CRD\n- HelmChart CRD\n- Bucket CRD\n- ExternalArtifact CRD\n- ArtifactGenerator CRD\n\n## Kustomize Controller\n**Description:** \"The GitOps Toolkit Kustomize Controller documentation.\"\n\n**Custom Resources:**\n- Kustomization CRD\n\n## Helm Controller\n**Description:** \"The GitOps Toolkit Helm Controller documentation.\"\n\n**Custom Resources:**\n- HelmRelease CRD\n\n## Notification Controller\n**Description:** \"The GitOps Toolkit Notification Controller documentation.\"\n\n**Custom Resources:**\n- Provider CRD\n- Alert CRD\n- Receiver CRD\n\n## Image Reflector and Automation Controllers\n**Description:** \"The GitOps Toolkit Image Automation Controllers documentation.\"\n\n**Custom Resources:**\n- ImageRepository CRD\n- ImagePolicy CRD\n- ImageUpdateAutomation CRD"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b4f5a06-4bc3-4221-b900-b8461cc3e79d","uuid":"2d206758-4d78-4d1d-afed-43be4caed97e","timestamp":"2026-08-31T10:04:42.755Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":161132,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Flux GitOps Toolkit Components\n\n## Source Controllers\n**Description:** \"The GitOps Toolkit Source Controllers documentation.\"\n\n**Custom Resources:**\n- GitRepository CRD\n- OCIRepository CRD\n- HelmRepository CRD\n- HelmChart CRD\n- Bucket CRD\n- ExternalArtifact CRD\n- ArtifactGenerator CRD\n\n## Kustomize Controller\n**Description:** \"The GitOps Toolkit Kustomize Controller documentation.\"\n\n**Custom Resources:**\n- Kustomization CRD\n\n## Helm Controller\n**Description:** \"The GitOps Toolkit Helm Controller documentation.\"\n\n**Custom Resources:**\n- HelmRelease CRD\n\n## Notification Controller\n**Description:** \"The GitOps Toolkit Notification Controller documentation.\"\n\n**Custom Resources:**\n- Provider CRD\n- Alert CRD\n- Receiver CRD\n\n## Image Reflector and Automation Controllers\n**Description:** \"The GitOps Toolkit Image Automation Controllers documentation.\"\n\n**Custom Resources:**\n- ImageRepository CRD\n- ImagePolicy CRD\n- ImageUpdateAutomation CRD","durationMs":3513,"url":"https://fluxcd.io/flux/components/"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014ZrB8bX5G5ZDkbzyUadYhE","type":"tool_result","content":"# Sync Phases and Waves - Key Content\n\n**Hook Types and Phases:**\n\nArgo CD recognizes seven hook types. Three primary phases structure deployment: \"PreSync\" hooks execute \"prior to the application of the manifests.\" \"Sync\" hooks run \"after all PreSync hooks completed and were successful, at the same time as the application of the manifests.\" \"PostSync\" hooks execute \"after all Sync hooks completed and were successful, a successful application, and all resources in a Healthy state.\"\n\nAdditionally, \"SyncFail\" hooks run \"when the sync operation fails.\"\n\n**Phase Execution Process:**\n\nDuring sync operations, Argo CD follows this sequence: first, all PreSync-marked resources are applied; if any fail, the entire process stops. Next, Sync-marked resources are applied; failures mark the operation as failed, and SyncFail hooks also execute. Finally, PostSync hooks run; their failure marks the deployment as failed.\n\n**Sync Waves Mechanism:**\n\nWaves are defined using the `argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave` annotation with integer values. \"Hooks and resources are assigned to wave 0 by default. The wave can be negative, so you can create a wave that runs before all other resources.\"\n\n**Ordering Algorithm:**\n\nWhen combining phases and waves, Argo CD orders resources by: \"1. The phase 2. The wave they are in (lower values first) 3. By kind 4. By name\"\n\n**Configuration Annotations:**\n\nUse `argocd.argoproj.io/hook: PreSync` for phase assignment and `argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave: \"5\"` for wave specification."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b4f5a06-4bc3-4221-b900-b8461cc3e79d","uuid":"239fa377-bdc2-4605-989c-ea7dfe058ab1","timestamp":"2026-08-31T10:04:43.981Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":23102,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Sync Phases and Waves - Key Content\n\n**Hook Types and Phases:**\n\nArgo CD recognizes seven hook types. Three primary phases structure deployment: \"PreSync\" hooks execute \"prior to the application of the manifests.\" \"Sync\" hooks run \"after all PreSync hooks completed and were successful, at the same time as the application of the manifests.\" \"PostSync\" hooks execute \"after all Sync hooks completed and were successful, a successful application, and all resources in a Healthy state.\"\n\nAdditionally, \"SyncFail\" hooks run \"when the sync operation fails.\"\n\n**Phase Execution Process:**\n\nDuring sync operations, Argo CD follows this sequence: first, all PreSync-marked resources are applied; if any fail, the entire process stops. Next, Sync-marked resources are applied; failures mark the operation as failed, and SyncFail hooks also execute. Finally, PostSync hooks run; their failure marks the deployment as failed.\n\n**Sync Waves Mechanism:**\n\nWaves are defined using the `argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave` annotation with integer values. \"Hooks and resources are assigned to wave 0 by default. The wave can be negative, so you can create a wave that runs before all other resources.\"\n\n**Ordering Algorithm:**\n\nWhen combining phases and waves, Argo CD orders resources by: \"1. The phase 2. The wave they are in (lower values first) 3. By kind 4. By name\"\n\n**Configuration Annotations:**\n\nUse `argocd.argoproj.io/hook: PreSync` for phase assignment and `argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave: \"5\"` for wave specification.","durationMs":5934,"url":"https://argo-cd.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user-guide/sync-waves/"}}
