{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TwZgNbhcYXLhzhVDPmaEdf","type":"tool_result","content":"# Argo CD Component Descriptions\n\n**API Server:**\n\"The API server is a gRPC/REST server which exposes the API consumed by the Web UI, CLI, and CI/CD systems.\"\n\nIts responsibilities include: \"application management and status reporting,\" \"invoking of application operations (e.g. sync, rollback, user-defined actions),\" \"repository and cluster credential management,\" \"authentication and auth delegation to external identity providers,\" \"RBAC enforcement,\" and serving as a \"listener/forwarder for Git webhook events.\"\n\n**Repository Server:**\n\"The repository server is an internal service which maintains a local cache of the Git repository holding the application manifests.\"\n\nIt is tasked with \"generating and returning the Kubernetes manifests when provided\" a repository URL, revision, application path, and template-specific configuration.\n\n**Application Controller:**\n\"The application controller is a Kubernetes controller which continuously monitors running applications and compares the current, live state against the desired target state (as specified in the repo).\"\n\nThe controller \"detects `OutOfSync` application state and optionally takes corrective action\" and bears responsibility for \"invoking any user-defined hooks for lifecycle events (PreSync, Sync, PostSync).\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b4f5a06-4bc3-4221-b900-b8461cc3e79d","uuid":"98435c8d-b027-43ed-a038-f06ba2ae0aa3","timestamp":"2026-08-31T10:04:54.878Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":10470,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Argo CD Component Descriptions\n\n**API Server:**\n\"The API server is a gRPC/REST server which exposes the API consumed by the Web UI, CLI, and CI/CD systems.\"\n\nIts responsibilities include: \"application management and status reporting,\" \"invoking of application operations (e.g. sync, rollback, user-defined actions),\" \"repository and cluster credential management,\" \"authentication and auth delegation to external identity providers,\" \"RBAC enforcement,\" and serving as a \"listener/forwarder for Git webhook events.\"\n\n**Repository Server:**\n\"The repository server is an internal service which maintains a local cache of the Git repository holding the application manifests.\"\n\nIt is tasked with \"generating and returning the Kubernetes manifests when provided\" a repository URL, revision, application path, and template-specific configuration.\n\n**Application Controller:**\n\"The application controller is a Kubernetes controller which continuously monitors running applications and compares the current, live state against the desired target state (as specified in the repo).\"\n\nThe controller \"detects `OutOfSync` application state and optionally takes corrective action\" and bears responsibility for \"invoking any user-defined hooks for lifecycle events (PreSync, Sync, PostSync).\"","durationMs":2881,"url":"https://argo-cd.readthedocs.io/en/stable/operator-manual/architecture/"}}
