{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BgkPB1XvJ3JDuXgBQHcThX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Argo Rollouts A/B testing strategy documentation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Argo Rollouts | Argo\",\"url\":\"https://argoproj.github.io/rollouts/\"},{\"title\":\"Experiments - Argo Rollouts - Kubernetes Progressive Delivery Controller\",\"url\":\"https://argo-rollouts.readthedocs.io/en/stable/features/experiment/\"},{\"title\":\"Best Practices - Argo Rollouts - Kubernetes Progressive Delivery Controller\",\"url\":\"https://argo-rollouts.readthedocs.io/en/stable/best-practices/\"},{\"title\":\"FAQ - Argo Rollouts - Kubernetes Progressive Delivery Controller\",\"url\":\"https://argo-rollouts.readthedocs.io/en/stable/FAQ/\"},{\"title\":\"Overview - Argo Rollouts - Kubernetes Progressive Delivery Controller\",\"url\":\"https://argo-rollouts.readthedocs.io/en/stable/features/analysis/\"},{\"title\":\"Argo Rollouts - Kubernetes Progressive Delivery Controller\",\"url\":\"https://argo-rollouts.readthedocs.io/\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Usage - Argo Rollouts - Kubernetes Progressive Delivery Controller\",\"url\":\"https://argo-rollouts.readthedocs.io/en/stable/getting-started/\"},{\"title\":\"Rollout Spec - Argo Rollouts - Kubernetes Progressive Delivery Controller\",\"url\":\"https://argo-rollouts.readthedocs.io/en/stable/features/specification/\"},{\"title\":\"Concepts - Argo Rollouts - Kubernetes Progressive Delivery Controller\",\"url\":\"https://argo-rollouts.readthedocs.io/en/stable/concepts/\"},{\"title\":\"Canary Deployment Strategy - Argo Rollouts\",\"url\":\"https://argo-rollouts.readthedocs.io/en/stable/features/canary/\"}]\n\nI've found comprehensive information about Argo Rollouts and its A/B testing strategy documentation. Here's what I discovered:\n\n## Argo Rollouts A/B Testing and Experimentation\n\nArgo Rollouts is a Kubernetes controller and set of CRDs which provide advanced deployment capabilities such as blue-green, canary, canary analysis, experimentation, and progressive delivery features to Kubernetes.\n\n### Experimentation and A/B Testing\n\nA rollout using the Canary strategy can create an experiment using an experiment step. The experiment step serves as a blocking step for the Rollout, and a Rollout will not continue until the Experiment succeeds.\n\nA Rollout using the Canary strategy along with Traffic Routing can split traffic to an experiment stack in a fine-grained manner. When Traffic Routing is enabled, the Rollout Experiment step allows traffic to be shifted to experiment pods.\n\n### Key Capabilities\n\nArgo Rollouts (optionally) integrates with ingress controllers and service meshes, leveraging their traffic shaping abilities to gradually shift traffic to the new version during an update. Additionally, Rollouts can query and interpret metrics from various providers to verify key KPIs and drive automated promotion or rollback during an update.\n\n### Analysis Integration\n\nArgo Rollouts provides several ways to perform analysis to drive progressive delivery. This document describes how to achieve various forms of progressive delivery, varying the point in time analysis is performed, its frequency, and occurrence.\n\nThe official documentation is available at the Argo Rollouts ReadTheDocs site, which includes detailed guides on experiments, analysis templates, and best practices for implementing A/B testing strategies.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b4f5a06-4bc3-4221-b900-b8461cc3e79d","uuid":"9ace4cb0-8421-42b9-869f-c3265e8c4266","timestamp":"2026-08-31T10:05:04.463Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Argo Rollouts A/B testing strategy documentation","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_019YRZAFWTPbVFRJG28Wb81a","content":[{"title":"Argo Rollouts | Argo","url":"https://argoproj.github.io/rollouts/"},{"title":"Experiments - Argo Rollouts - Kubernetes Progressive Delivery Controller","url":"https://argo-rollouts.readthedocs.io/en/stable/features/experiment/"},{"title":"Best Practices - Argo Rollouts - Kubernetes Progressive Delivery Controller","url":"https://argo-rollouts.readthedocs.io/en/stable/best-practices/"},{"title":"FAQ - Argo Rollouts - Kubernetes Progressive Delivery Controller","url":"https://argo-rollouts.readthedocs.io/en/stable/FAQ/"},{"title":"Overview - Argo Rollouts - Kubernetes Progressive Delivery Controller","url":"https://argo-rollouts.readthedocs.io/en/stable/features/analysis/"},{"title":"Argo Rollouts - Kubernetes Progressive Delivery Controller","url":"https://argo-rollouts.readthedocs.io/"},{"title":"Basic Usage - Argo Rollouts - Kubernetes Progressive Delivery Controller","url":"https://argo-rollouts.readthedocs.io/en/stable/getting-started/"},{"title":"Rollout Spec - Argo Rollouts - Kubernetes Progressive Delivery Controller","url":"https://argo-rollouts.readthedocs.io/en/stable/features/specification/"},{"title":"Concepts - Argo Rollouts - Kubernetes Progressive Delivery Controller","url":"https://argo-rollouts.readthedocs.io/en/stable/concepts/"},{"title":"Canary Deployment Strategy - Argo Rollouts","url":"https://argo-rollouts.readthedocs.io/en/stable/features/canary/"}]},"I've found comprehensive information about Argo Rollouts and its A/B testing strategy documentation. Here's what I discovered:\n\n## Argo Rollouts A/B Testing and Experimentation\n\nArgo Rollouts is a Kubernetes controller and set of CRDs which provide advanced deployment capabilities such as blue-green, canary, canary analysis, experimentation, and progressive delivery features to Kubernetes.\n\n### Experimentation and A/B Testing\n\nA rollout using the Canary strategy can create an experiment using an experiment step. The experiment step serves as a blocking step for the Rollout, and a Rollout will not continue until the Experiment succeeds.\n\nA Rollout using the Canary strategy along with Traffic Routing can split traffic to an experiment stack in a fine-grained manner. When Traffic Routing is enabled, the Rollout Experiment step allows traffic to be shifted to experiment pods.\n\n### Key Capabilities\n\nArgo Rollouts (optionally) integrates with ingress controllers and service meshes, leveraging their traffic shaping abilities to gradually shift traffic to the new version during an update. Additionally, Rollouts can query and interpret metrics from various providers to verify key KPIs and drive automated promotion or rollback during an update.\n\n### Analysis Integration\n\nArgo Rollouts provides several ways to perform analysis to drive progressive delivery. This document describes how to achieve various forms of progressive delivery, varying the point in time analysis is performed, its frequency, and occurrence.\n\nThe official documentation is available at the Argo Rollouts ReadTheDocs site, which includes detailed guides on experiments, analysis templates, and best practices for implementing A/B testing strategies."],"durationSeconds":7.672920400000002,"searchCount":1}}
