{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QKLY8Q8FTkg9HiXcb1aQ1b","type":"tool_result","content":"# Argo CD Tracking and Deployment Strategies - Key Quotes\n\n**Opening prose on tracking strategies:**\n\"An Argo CD application spec provides several different ways of tracking Kubernetes resource manifests.\"\n\n**Branch/HEAD Tracking:**\n\"If a branch name or a symbolic reference (like HEAD) is specified, Argo CD will continually compare live state against the resource manifests defined at the tip of the specified branch or the resolved commit of the symbolic reference.\"\n\n**Tag Tracking:**\n\"If a tag is specified, the manifests at the specified Git tag will be used to perform the sync comparison.\"\n\n**Commit Pinning description:**\n\"If a Git commit SHA is specified, the app is effectively pinned to the manifests defined at the specified commit.\"\n\n**Key distinction on mutability:**\n\"Since commit SHAs cannot change meaning, the only way to change the live state of an app which is pinned to a commit, is by updating the tracking revision in the application to a different commit containing the new manifests.\"\n\n**Contrast implicit in strategies:**\nTags are \"generally considered more stable, and less frequently updated\" compared to branches, which track continuously."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b4f5a06-4bc3-4221-b900-b8461cc3e79d","uuid":"664ef41d-8995-4861-9e00-3cc2f8c90b5f","timestamp":"2026-08-31T10:06:44.368Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":17681,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Argo CD Tracking and Deployment Strategies - Key Quotes\n\n**Opening prose on tracking strategies:**\n\"An Argo CD application spec provides several different ways of tracking Kubernetes resource manifests.\"\n\n**Branch/HEAD Tracking:**\n\"If a branch name or a symbolic reference (like HEAD) is specified, Argo CD will continually compare live state against the resource manifests defined at the tip of the specified branch or the resolved commit of the symbolic reference.\"\n\n**Tag Tracking:**\n\"If a tag is specified, the manifests at the specified Git tag will be used to perform the sync comparison.\"\n\n**Commit Pinning description:**\n\"If a Git commit SHA is specified, the app is effectively pinned to the manifests defined at the specified commit.\"\n\n**Key distinction on mutability:**\n\"Since commit SHAs cannot change meaning, the only way to change the live state of an app which is pinned to a commit, is by updating the tracking revision in the application to a different commit containing the new manifests.\"\n\n**Contrast implicit in strategies:**\nTags are \"generally considered more stable, and less frequently updated\" compared to branches, which track continuously.","durationMs":3923,"url":"https://argo-cd.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user-guide/tracking_strategies/"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019DT8yUy7JSBbPTxJp69826","type":"tool_result","content":"# Kustomization API: Key Definitions\n\n**API Purpose:**\n\"The `Kustomization` API defines a pipeline for fetching, decrypting, building, validating and applying Kustomize overlays or plain Kubernetes manifests.\"\n\n**Reconciliation Interval:**\n\"`.spec.interval` is a required field that specifies the interval at which the Kustomization is reconciled, i.e. the controller fetches the source with the Kubernetes manifests, builds the Kustomization and applies it on the cluster, correcting any existing drift in the process. The minimum value should be 60 seconds.\"\n\nNo default interval value is specified; only a minimum requirement is stated.\n\n**Garbage Collection:**\n\"`.spec.prune` is a required boolean field to enable/disable garbage collection for a Kustomization. Garbage collection means that the Kubernetes objects that were previously applied on the cluster but are missing from the current source revision, are removed from the cluster automatically.\"\n\n**Service Account Impersonation:**\n\"`.spec.serviceAccountName` is an optional field used to specify the ServiceAccount to be impersonated while reconciling the Kustomization.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b4f5a06-4bc3-4221-b900-b8461cc3e79d","uuid":"4d954599-a020-464f-90a0-a46e213f1f6f","timestamp":"2026-08-31T10:06:46.897Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":408211,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Kustomization API: Key Definitions\n\n**API Purpose:**\n\"The `Kustomization` API defines a pipeline for fetching, decrypting, building, validating and applying Kustomize overlays or plain Kubernetes manifests.\"\n\n**Reconciliation Interval:**\n\"`.spec.interval` is a required field that specifies the interval at which the Kustomization is reconciled, i.e. the controller fetches the source with the Kubernetes manifests, builds the Kustomization and applies it on the cluster, correcting any existing drift in the process. The minimum value should be 60 seconds.\"\n\nNo default interval value is specified; only a minimum requirement is stated.\n\n**Garbage Collection:**\n\"`.spec.prune` is a required boolean field to enable/disable garbage collection for a Kustomization. Garbage collection means that the Kubernetes objects that were previously applied on the cluster but are missing from the current source revision, are removed from the cluster automatically.\"\n\n**Service Account Impersonation:**\n\"`.spec.serviceAccountName` is an optional field used to specify the ServiceAccount to be impersonated while reconciling the Kustomization.\"","durationMs":4749,"url":"https://fluxcd.io/flux/components/kustomize/kustomizations/"}}
