{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QWkUS4vxJJG2CuDL15g9Uo","type":"tool_result","content":"After carefully reviewing the Flux FAQ page, I must report that **none of the topics you requested appear on this page**. There is no discussion of:\n\n- Pull-based vs push-based delivery\n- Why an agent runs inside the cluster\n- Cluster credentials\n- How Flux differs from a CI system pushing with kubectl\n\nHowever, the FAQ does address reconciliation and drift. Here are the relevant questions that DO appear:\n\n**On reconciliation:**\n\"What is a Kustomization reconciliation?\" explains that reconciliation can mean \"applying changes on the cluster\" and \"garbage collection of resources removed from Git,\" with the interval representing \"the interval at which you want to undo manual changes.\"\n\n**On drift detection:**\nThe installation configuration menu references \"Helm drift detection\" as an available feature, though the actual FAQ content doesn't discuss this topic in detail.\n\nThe page primarily focuses on Kustomize workflows, Helm releases, and migration guidance rather than architectural questions about deployment models."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b4f5a06-4bc3-4221-b900-b8461cc3e79d","uuid":"541b8294-f86b-4ddb-b70b-8e0ec2fb3c68","timestamp":"2026-08-31T10:07:26.985Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":233860,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"After carefully reviewing the Flux FAQ page, I must report that **none of the topics you requested appear on this page**. There is no discussion of:\n\n- Pull-based vs push-based delivery\n- Why an agent runs inside the cluster\n- Cluster credentials\n- How Flux differs from a CI system pushing with kubectl\n\nHowever, the FAQ does address reconciliation and drift. Here are the relevant questions that DO appear:\n\n**On reconciliation:**\n\"What is a Kustomization reconciliation?\" explains that reconciliation can mean \"applying changes on the cluster\" and \"garbage collection of resources removed from Git,\" with the interval representing \"the interval at which you want to undo manual changes.\"\n\n**On drift detection:**\nThe installation configuration menu references \"Helm drift detection\" as an available feature, though the actual FAQ content doesn't discuss this topic in detail.\n\nThe page primarily focuses on Kustomize workflows, Helm releases, and migration guidance rather than architectural questions about deployment models.","durationMs":3810,"url":"https://fluxcd.io/flux/faq/"}}
