{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016Y8cBe8nAtMs6SsXhQJB6F","type":"tool_result","content":"# Argo CD Out-of-Sync Determination\n\nAccording to the documentation, here is the opening explanation:\n\n\"It is possible for an application to be `OutOfSync` even immediately after a successful Sync operation.\"\n\nThe page then lists several reasons why this occurs, including manifest bugs with unknown fields, disabled pruning leaving resources to delete, controller/webhook alterations, Helm template functions generating different data, and HPA controller reordering of metrics specifications.\n\nThe core concept is that Argo CD compares the desired state (from Git manifests) against the live state (what actually exists in the Kubernetes cluster). When these states diverge, the application shows as out of sync."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b4f5a06-4bc3-4221-b900-b8461cc3e79d","uuid":"cac72245-8db8-4147-bbd5-dc76cefa0626","timestamp":"2026-08-31T10:07:29.648Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":16861,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Argo CD Out-of-Sync Determination\n\nAccording to the documentation, here is the opening explanation:\n\n\"It is possible for an application to be `OutOfSync` even immediately after a successful Sync operation.\"\n\nThe page then lists several reasons why this occurs, including manifest bugs with unknown fields, disabled pruning leaving resources to delete, controller/webhook alterations, Helm template functions generating different data, and HPA controller reordering of metrics specifications.\n\nThe core concept is that Argo CD compares the desired state (from Git manifests) against the live state (what actually exists in the Kubernetes cluster). When these states diverge, the application shows as out of sync.","durationMs":2944,"url":"https://argo-cd.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user-guide/diffing/"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017caLrQ8RUk28WpLXMEthQP","type":"tool_result","content":"# OpenGitOps Documents Repository\n\n## Root-Level Files\n\nBased on the repository structure shown, the exact file names in the root directory are:\n\n- CONTRIBUTING.md\n- GLOSSARY.md\n- LICENSE.md\n- PRINCIPLES.md\n- README.md\n\n## Repository Description\n\nAccording to the README, this repository contains: \"Lasting documents from the OpenGitOps project which are versioned and released together (including the GitOps Principles and Glossary)\"\n\nThe repository also notes that it includes translations in an `i18n` folder and maintains a `reference` directory with author attribution for different release versions."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b4f5a06-4bc3-4221-b900-b8461cc3e79d","uuid":"1e00a899-58a1-4d22-bd68-32af547fcc01","timestamp":"2026-08-31T10:07:36.288Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":277547,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# OpenGitOps Documents Repository\n\n## Root-Level Files\n\nBased on the repository structure shown, the exact file names in the root directory are:\n\n- CONTRIBUTING.md\n- GLOSSARY.md\n- LICENSE.md\n- PRINCIPLES.md\n- README.md\n\n## Repository Description\n\nAccording to the README, this repository contains: \"Lasting documents from the OpenGitOps project which are versioned and released together (including the GitOps Principles and Glossary)\"\n\nThe repository also notes that it includes translations in an `i18n` folder and maintains a `reference` directory with author attribution for different release versions.","durationMs":10986,"url":"https://github.com/open-gitops/documents"}}
